# Dependencies
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build output
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# Rayfin deployment state — tenant/workspace GUIDs and the publishable key.
# PLAN §2.1 decision 12 sends this repo to a public template, so none of it ships.
rayfin/.env
rayfin/.deployments.json
rayfin/.lockfile.json
rayfin/.temp/

# Test output
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright-mcp/

# Raw, cached and derived geodata. Large, redownloadable, and — for AIS — carrying identifiers.
# See NOTICE.md for every source. `data/derived` is listed EXPLICITLY: in a sibling repo an
# ignore list held raw/interim/cache/curated but not derived, so moving a sensitive file out of
# the deploy quietly committed it to git instead. Same data, same rule, different hole.
#
# ⚠️ Anchored to the repo root on purpose. A bare `data/` also matches `rayfin/data/`, which holds
# the Rayfin schema the template guidelines require — and the symptom is a fresh clone that does
# not compile, not a missing-file error.
/data/
/data/derived/
*.laz
*.las
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gml
*.xyz
*.zip

# Generated browser assets. Tens of megabytes and reproducible from open sources at any time with
# `python tools/geodata/pipeline.py`, which is why the app must show a setup notice rather than a
# blank canvas on a fresh clone.
public/terrain/
public/tracks/
*.ktx2
*.glb

# Local scratch
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
temp/
scratch/
*.log
.vscode/settings.json

test-results/
playwright-report/

# Output of tools/ops/recover_image_source.py
.recovered/
